{"status":"completed","summary":"The staged help site is running persistently on node1 port 8080. Legacy `/manual/` URLs permanently redirect to `/help/` while preserving path and query strings, and `/status.txt` remains directly accessible.","actions_performed":["Installed a Python 3.5-compatible static HTTP service without changing the operating system or kernel.","Configured HTTP 301 redirects from `/manual` to `/help`.","Enabled the service through systemd under the unprivileged `nobody` account.","Restarted node1 and verified service, content, redirects, OS, and kernel recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Serve the staged help tree on TCP port 8080.","command_ids":["cmd-9c9501b0d7ee46d2","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd"],"summary":"The service listens on port 8080 and returns the staged root and nested help documents with HTTP 200, including after restart."},{"requirement":"Permanently redirect old manual URLs while retaining path and query string.","command_ids":["cmd-c2e0926ae4a64663","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd"],"summary":"Requests return HTTP 301; `/manual/network/setup.html?mode=compact&lang=en` maps to the corresponding `/help/` URL with its query unchanged."},{"requirement":"Return `/status.txt` directly without redirect.","command_ids":["cmd-9c9501b0d7ee46d2","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd"],"summary":"The status document returns HTTP 200 with the supplied content before and after restart."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel.","command_ids":["cmd-c9a589a5758241de","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd"],"summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 LTS and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged."},{"requirement":"Restart node1 and prove persistent recovery.","command_ids":["cmd-104d5b5ca0024b19","cmd-b28ad33c1fd24c6b","cmd-73e58685fc0140fb","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd"],"summary":"Captured healthy baseline boot ID and content hashes, acknowledged the scheduled native reboot, observed the changed boot ID, and verified the enabled service, listener, identical content hashes, HTTP